# The build context is src/categorizer, so this file only has to think about
# what is in here -- unlike the root .dockerignore, which guards a whole
# repository.
#
# The pattern rules are Docker's, not git's: no-slash means the root of the
# context and `*` does not cross a `/`, which is the difference that cost a leak
# to learn in #23. Hence `**/` on everything that could appear at depth.

# .venv is the one with teeth. It is built on Windows, its scripts carry
# absolute Windows paths, and the image builds its own at /app/.venv -- so a
# copy of this one is not merely useless, it would shadow the real thing at the
# same path.
.venv/

**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
tests/
**/.env
**/.env.*
